---
import '../styles/prose.css';

import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { getApp } from '../data/apps';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const app = getApp('convertit')!;
const appPath = `/apps/${app.slug}/`;

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-11-04T15:44:10Z');
const lastUpdatedDisplay = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  hour: '2-digit',
  minute: '2-digit',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
  timeZoneName: 'short',
}).format(lastUpdated);

const title = `${app.name} terms of service`;
const description =
  'Terms of service for Convertit by The Byte Array Ltd: a free offline audio and video converter, your licence, your files stay on your device, and your statutory rights.';
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Apps', path: '/apps/' },
    { name: app.name, path: appPath },
    { name: 'Terms of service', path: Astro.url.pathname },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-4 sm:pt-10" data-pagefind-body>
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { label: 'Apps', href: '/apps/' },
        { label: app.name, href: appPath },
        { label: 'Terms of service' },
      ]}
    />

    <header class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,7.5vw,3.75rem)] leading-[1.04] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance"
      >
        {title}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-label-lg text-on-surface-variant">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString()}>{lastUpdatedDisplay}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit (“the App”) is published by {site.company.name}, a company registered in{' '}
          {site.company.jurisdiction} (company number{' '}
          <a href={site.company.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link">{site.company.number}</a>),
          with its registered office at {site.company.office}. In these terms, “we” and “us” mean{' '}
          {site.company.name}, and “you” means the person using the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>These terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms govern your use of the App. By installing or using it, you agree to them. If you do not
          agree, do not use the App. They sit alongside our{' '}
          <a href={app.privacyPath} class="text-link">privacy policy</a>, which is part of your agreement with
          us. Our <a href="/terms/" class="text-link">site terms</a> cover this website. Where the two differ,
          these terms apply to the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the App does</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit is a free, offline audio and video converter for Android. You pick a file and a format
          (MP3, M4A, AAC, OGG or OPUS) and it converts on your device, in the background, and it can edit the
          tags and cover art. It shows no ads. The current features are listed under What it does on the{' '}
          <a href={appPath} class="text-link">Convertit page</a>. A separate paid app,{' '}
          <a href="/apps/convertit-pro/" class="text-link">Convertit Pro</a>, offers more tools.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Price</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit is free. There is no purchase, no subscription, no in-app charges and no ads. If we ever
          offer paid features, we will say so clearly before any charge.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your licence</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit is free to download and use. We give you a personal, non-transferable, non-exclusive
          licence to install and use the App on devices you control, for your own use. You may not sell, rent,
          sub-license or redistribute the App, or copy it except as normal use and the law allow.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may not reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the App, except where applicable law
          expressly permits it (for example, to achieve interoperability). The App may include open-source
          components that are licensed to you under their own licences. Nothing in these terms limits or
          overrides your rights under those licences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your files</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of the files you open and the files the App produces. The App processes your
          files on your device and does not upload them to us or to anyone else. You are responsible for
          keeping your own backups and for having the right to use the files you process. See our{' '}
          <a href={app.privacyPath} class="text-link">privacy policy</a> for how the App handles data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Updates and support</h2>
        <p>
          We fix what we advertise. Contact us with your device and Android version and steps to reproduce the
          problem. We aim to reply within 5 business days and to fix it or provide a workaround within 14
          business days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Warranties and your statutory rights</h2>
        <p>
          We provide the App with reasonable care and skill, but we cannot promise it is error-free or that it
          will run on every device or with every file. As far as the law allows, the App is provided “as is”
          and we exclude other warranties and conditions that would otherwise apply. None of this affects any
          statutory rights you have that cannot be excluded.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our liability</h2>
        <p>
          We do not exclude or limit our liability where it would be unlawful to do so. This includes
          liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, and, if you are a
          consumer, for damage to your device or to other digital content caused by our failure to use
          reasonable care and skill.
        </p>
        <p>
          Subject to that, and because the App is provided free of charge, we are not liable for loss that was
          not reasonably foreseeable, for loss of data you could have backed up, or for indirect or
          consequential loss.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using the App at any time by uninstalling it. We may end your licence only if you
          materially breach these terms. If your licence ends, you must stop using the App. Your statutory
          rights are not affected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We version this page. See the Last updated date and time above. If we make a material change, we add
          a dated note here and announce it on our blog at least 7 days before it takes effect. Continuing to
          use the App after a change takes effect means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and disputes are subject to the courts of
          England and Wales. If you are a consumer living in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you can also bring
          proceedings in your local courts, and you keep the benefit of any mandatory consumer protections
          that apply where you live.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms use our{' '}
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or email us at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
